                <pb facs="0822" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg708"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.51/710: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-27T16:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:15
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>13. To-day’s press published Executive decree signed on 26th regulating issuance
                    and amortization of bonds of public agrarian debt based on article 7 of the law
                    of January 10, 1920. The decree provides for issuance of five series of ten
                    million pesos each 5 percent bonds which will be amortized by means of annual
                    drawings of one-twentieth of value on the bonds outstanding each January.
                    Application of claimants must be presented within one year. Value of
                    expropriated land will in no case be fixed at a price greater than its fiscal
                    value as registered where the property is located plus 10 percent. Copy of
                    decree by mail.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d610-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
